      en: "The Krushuna Waterfalls are located in the village of Krushuna, central northern Bulgaria, and consist of a system of cascades up to 15 meters high, formed by limestone deposits. The water flows over several terraces, creating small pools suitable for bathing. The waterfalls are surrounded by dense greenery, including mosses, ferns, and rare orchids. The surrounding landscape is part of the region's karst area and offers hiking trails to the waterfalls and nearby caves. The Krushuna Waterfalls are a popular destination, especially in spring when snowmelt increases water flow. The area is also known for its bird diversity.",
